  "answer": "No, you do not have to pay for an extra legroom seat. The policy states that extra legroom seats cost EUR 25 (short-haul), EUR 35 (medium-haul), or EUR 50 (long-haul) per flight for all passengers in the economy cabin, including Flex passengers. However, since you are on a Flex fare, you are eligible for free seat selection as per the policy. If you choose an extra legroom seat, you will still need to pay the applicable fee for that seat type.",
